# ideas.md stays current

`ideas.md` is the backlog. When you **implement** an item from that file as a real feature, **delete that item** in the same change — do not leave it listed as future work.

## What counts as “implemented”

- The feature works in the app (not just a plan or stub)
- README is updated if the behavior is user-facing (see readme-keeps-pace rule)

## What to remove

- Delete the bullet (or section) that described the shipped idea
- If a research section only existed to support that idea and nothing else references it, trim or remove the orphaned section too
- Keep **Done / won’t do** and **Explicitly out of scope** entries as-is unless the decision changed

## What not to do

- Do not delete ideas for partial work, spikes, or “coming soon” placeholders
- Do not delete **Safety (shipped)** or historical notes unless you're replacing them with something accurate

## Example

Shipping “Backup nudge on open” → remove the **Backup nudge on open** bullet under Import / export; tighten Scheduled backup (research) if it no longer lists that as planned work.
